WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.600
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:08.870 --> 00:11.705
The palualo ritual of the Ilokano people stems

3
00:11.706 --> 00:14.666
from their pre-Christian animistic beliefs,

4
00:14.667 --> 00:18.170
where ancestral and nature spirits were central to life.

5
00:18.171 --> 00:19.588
Similar to the atang,

6
00:19.589 --> 00:24.051
it appeases spirits to ensure harmony, health, and prosperity.

7
00:24.052 --> 00:26.094
Even with the spread of Christianity,

8
00:26.095 --> 00:27.763
these practices persist,

9
00:27.764 --> 00:30.348
blending Catholic elements with tradition.

10
00:30.349 --> 00:33.894
Calling out names of departed loved ones during a palualo

11
00:33.895 --> 00:37.439
ties ancestral remembrance to preventing misfortune,

12
00:37.440 --> 00:40.443
curing illnesses, and expressing gratitude.

13
00:48.326 --> 00:52.329
It reflects the Ilokano view of the interconnected realms of the living,

14
00:52.330 --> 00:53.122
the dead,

15
00:53.122 --> 00:53.915
and the spiritual,

16
00:53.916 --> 00:58.795
uniting families, preserving traditions, and affirming their identity.

17
01:10.973 --> 01:11.973
Ugly!

18
01:14.435 --> 01:15.520
Ugly!

19
01:17.897 --> 01:19.314
Hey, ugly!

20
01:19.315 --> 01:20.690
Let me enter.

21
01:20.691 --> 01:23.276
I swear to God, if I see you naked...

22
01:23.277 --> 01:24.736
I'm telling you.

23
01:24.737 --> 01:26.489
I will hit you.

24
01:27.949 --> 01:29.450
Ugly!

25
01:31.911 --> 01:34.162
Did I tell you to come in?

26
01:34.163 --> 01:36.039
Your dad is looking for you.

27
01:36.040 --> 01:38.042
What happened to you?

28
01:41.254 --> 01:43.714
I just have a lot on my mind.

29
01:45.967 --> 01:47.926
You know, Jorge...

30
01:47.927 --> 01:50.011
We're still young.

31
01:50.012 --> 01:52.055
We still have a lot of time.

32
01:52.056 --> 01:55.308
That's why... let's not think of ourselves for now.

33
01:55.309 --> 01:58.812
Our duty now is to be present for the adults.

34
01:58.813 --> 02:03.775
For them, they have a shorter time left to grieve.

35
02:03.776 --> 02:04.735
That's why, come on.

36
02:04.736 --> 02:06.404
Get up.

37
02:06.737 --> 02:08.739
What are you talking about?

38
02:10.283 --> 02:11.283
Come on.

39
02:11.284 --> 02:12.909
Spill the tea.

40
02:12.910 --> 02:15.288
What happened between you and Kiko?

41
02:25.089 --> 02:26.882
Kiko's leaving me.

42
02:26.883 --> 02:28.008
What?

43
02:28.009 --> 02:29.092
That was fast.

44
02:29.093 --> 02:30.927
You're not even official yet.

45
02:30.928 --> 02:32.762
He's going to Manila.

46
02:32.763 --> 02:34.557
He's going to study there.

47
02:35.057 --> 02:37.058
My God, Jorge.

48
02:37.059 --> 02:39.437
I know, I know.

49
02:40.104 --> 02:43.106
The first one to fall, loses.

50
02:43.107 --> 02:44.858
Forget that.

51
02:44.859 --> 02:47.694
Why are you listening to a fool like me?

52
02:47.695 --> 02:49.446
Isn't that what you're gonna say?

53
02:49.447 --> 02:50.822
No.

54
02:50.823 --> 02:52.741
I was going to say...

55
02:52.742 --> 02:55.619
It's better to have loved and lost...

56
02:55.620 --> 02:57.538
That's it.

57
03:01.250 --> 03:04.045
Why would I listen to you?

58
03:05.087 --> 03:06.379
When...

59
03:06.380 --> 03:08.966
You’re a fool.

60
03:09.717 --> 03:11.843
See, you're not the fool.

61
03:11.844 --> 03:13.304
I am.

62
03:13.888 --> 03:15.681
Good thing you know.

63
03:16.974 --> 03:19.267
Do you think you're the main character?

64
03:19.268 --> 03:21.770
I also have my life.

65
03:21.771 --> 03:23.480
Remember Cutie?

66
03:23.481 --> 03:25.107
They confessed.

67
03:25.608 --> 03:29.444
It's why I have a different perspective on love now.

68
03:29.445 --> 03:30.446
Sweet.

69
03:30.905 --> 03:32.073
Amazing.

70
03:32.365 --> 03:33.866
- And... - Fine.

71
03:35.076 --> 03:36.368
Well, excuse me.

72
03:36.369 --> 03:38.328
I'm only a supporting character.

73
03:38.329 --> 03:40.830
Yes, supporting character.

74
03:40.831 --> 03:42.375
That's why, Jorge.

75
03:43.084 --> 03:46.045
You need to fight for who you love.

76
03:46.879 --> 03:48.546
What did you say?

77
03:48.547 --> 03:49.965
You need to...

78
03:49.966 --> 03:51.467
Fight for who you love.

79
03:52.635 --> 03:53.677
You already know.

80
03:53.678 --> 03:56.763
Why do you have to make me repeat it?

81
03:56.764 --> 03:57.473
Ruth.

82
03:57.474 --> 03:59.141
That was the problem with Grandpa.

83
03:59.934 --> 04:01.227
He didn't fight for it.

84
04:02.436 --> 04:03.728
Grandpa?

85
04:03.729 --> 04:04.981
Huh?

86
04:06.482 --> 04:08.275
Obscenity!

87
04:08.276 --> 04:10.318
Oh, you're wearing shorts.

88
04:10.319 --> 04:12.696
Of course, it was hard back then.

89
04:12.697 --> 04:14.948
It was a different time then.

90
04:14.949 --> 04:16.157
There were lots of evil people.

91
04:16.158 --> 04:17.492
Close-minded.

92
04:17.493 --> 04:18.910
But even then...

93
04:18.911 --> 04:21.121
You have to be brave.

94
04:21.122 --> 04:22.581
Huh?

95
04:23.916 --> 04:25.792
We have to take charge.

96
04:25.793 --> 04:27.002
What are you saying?

97
04:27.003 --> 04:28.003
Ruth.

98
04:28.004 --> 04:29.421
Thank you.

99
04:29.422 --> 04:32.008
I’m going to Kiko.

100
04:34.302 --> 04:35.845
I'm going.

101
04:37.096 --> 04:38.597
Oh.

102
04:38.598 --> 04:41.392
People in love are crazy.

103
04:44.061 --> 04:45.903
It's a good thing you were able to visit.

104
04:45.928 --> 04:50.529
Yes. Our car even broke down. We travelled so far and we got stuck in traffic.

105
04:53.237 --> 04:54.654
Jorge.

106
04:54.655 --> 04:56.031
Later, Dad.

107
04:56.032 --> 04:57.574
I'm in a hurry.

108
04:57.575 --> 04:58.826
Jorge.

109
04:59.160 --> 05:00.369
Was that your son?

110
05:08.627 --> 05:10.129
He's my son.

111
05:17.511 --> 05:19.180
Jorge!

112
05:29.000 --> 05:32.500
"All the Things I Leave You" (Episode 6)

113
05:34.820 --> 05:36.613
Kiko?

114
05:36.614 --> 05:37.906
Is anyone here?

115
05:37.907 --> 05:39.492
Kiko?

116
05:39.867 --> 05:42.118
Kiko, come out.

117
05:42.119 --> 05:43.996
Kiko!

118
05:46.415 --> 05:47.917
Jasmine.

119
05:48.542 --> 05:49.918
Do you still remember me?

120
05:49.919 --> 05:52.546
Manong Kiko's boyfriend?

121
05:54.090 --> 05:55.508
Yes.

122
05:56.008 --> 05:57.425
Where is he?

123
05:57.426 --> 05:58.885
He went out.

124
05:58.886 --> 06:00.553
Where did he go?

125
06:00.554 --> 06:02.306
To the moon.

126
06:02.890 --> 06:03.557
Moon?

127
06:03.558 --> 06:09.480
Jasmine meant... Mun... Municipal hall.

128
06:11.107 --> 06:13.108
Oh, at the municipal hall.

129
06:13.109 --> 06:15.819
He had to attend to something there.

130
06:15.820 --> 06:17.947
Color ship.

131
06:20.282 --> 06:22.450
Oh, scholarship.

132
06:22.451 --> 06:23.618
Okay.

133
06:23.619 --> 06:25.955
I'll go find your cousin.

134
06:26.789 --> 06:27.914
Thank you.

135
06:27.915 --> 06:29.917
You're welcome.

136
06:31.001 --> 06:32.837
I'll go now.

137
06:42.054 --> 06:43.054
Manong!

138
06:43.973 --> 06:44.598
Oops!

139
06:44.599 --> 06:46.474
Gotcha!

140
06:46.475 --> 06:47.935
Sorry, Nate.

141
06:48.227 --> 06:50.271
I'm in a hurry.

142
06:50.646 --> 06:51.397
I noticed.

143
06:51.398 --> 06:52.897
You kept passing by earlier.

144
06:52.898 --> 06:54.900
You weren't even hearing me.

145
06:55.317 --> 06:57.277
I will go to Kiko and...

146
06:57.278 --> 06:58.654
I need to go.

147
06:59.864 --> 07:01.114
I noticed.

148
07:01.115 --> 07:02.575
You're always with him.

149
07:03.117 --> 07:04.243
Jorge.

150
07:04.785 --> 07:07.954
I know you always got a lot on your mind these days.

151
07:07.955 --> 07:09.915
Because your grandfather passed.

152
07:09.969 --> 07:11.344
If you need someone to talk to,

153
07:11.368 --> 07:13.204
I'm always here, you know.

154
07:19.884 --> 07:21.634
Nathan, come on!

155
07:21.635 --> 07:23.428
Get him over here.

156
07:23.429 --> 07:25.222
He's taking so long.

157
07:27.016 --> 07:27.850
I'll see you.

158
07:27.851 --> 07:29.810
Yes, I need to go.

159
07:47.953 --> 07:48.787
Excuse me.

160
07:48.788 --> 07:51.164
Where is the scholarship application?

161
07:51.165 --> 07:52.165
Over there.

162
07:52.166 --> 07:53.501
Thank you.

163
08:02.635 --> 08:03.636
Kiko!

164
08:04.887 --> 08:05.679
Kiko.

165
08:05.679 --> 08:06.347
Jorge?

166
08:06.348 --> 08:07.722
Don't go.

167
08:07.723 --> 08:08.599
Huh?

168
08:08.600 --> 08:10.934
Our grandfathers...

169
08:10.935 --> 08:13.896
They parted and never saw each other again.

170
08:15.231 --> 08:20.110
We have to right their wrongs in the past.

171
08:21.153 --> 08:21.862
Jorge.

172
08:21.863 --> 08:25.406
When I become the manager of the restaurant,

173
08:25.407 --> 08:28.952
You can be my assistant manager. You can...

174
08:28.953 --> 08:29.995
Jorge!

175
08:32.248 --> 08:33.791
You're so selfish!

176
08:35.459 --> 08:37.335
Don’t you get it?

177
08:37.336 --> 08:40.005
There are a lot of things I want to do in my life.

178
08:41.382 --> 08:43.384
I want to study in Manila.

179
08:45.135 --> 08:48.180
Opportunities like this are rare for me, Jorge.

180
08:49.014 --> 08:50.975
Why would I stay here?

181
08:53.519 --> 08:55.895
Who told you...

182
08:55.896 --> 08:58.524
that I wanted to be your assistant manager?

183
09:00.276 --> 09:00.985
I thought...

184
09:00.986 --> 09:03.362
Our grandparents did the right thing.

185
09:04.738 --> 09:07.157
We have our own paths in life.

186
09:08.242 --> 09:10.703
They only chose what was right for them.

187
09:11.704 --> 09:13.121
No...

188
09:13.122 --> 09:14.540
Next!

189
09:18.127 --> 09:19.670
I'm next.

190
09:20.879 --> 09:22.339
Jorge...

191
09:23.007 --> 09:25.175
Go home.

192
09:26.010 --> 09:27.386
Isn't it...

193
09:28.220 --> 09:30.764
Grandpa Tino's funeral today?

194
09:34.059 --> 09:35.603
You’re next!

195
11:03.982 --> 11:10.698
SOON TO REOPEN

196
11:20.916 --> 11:22.375
Let's clean up here.

197
11:22.376 --> 11:24.043
It's heavy.

198
11:24.044 --> 11:25.670
I'll help you.

199
11:25.671 --> 11:27.965
Put it here.

200
11:29.967 --> 11:31.718
That's good already.

201
11:31.719 --> 11:33.469
Here, Jorge.

202
11:33.470 --> 11:35.722
There's a lot to do here.

203
11:35.723 --> 11:37.224
Yes, actually.

204
11:39.935 --> 11:40.728
Here, put it here.

205
11:40.728 --> 11:41.395
No.

206
11:41.396 --> 11:42.396
Okay, okay.

207
11:43.814 --> 11:45.773
Okay.

208
11:45.774 --> 11:48.860
I'll go clean in the kitchen since there's a lot to fix there.

209
11:48.861 --> 11:50.696
- Stay here, okay? - Yes, okay.

210
12:04.001 --> 12:05.294
Jorge.

211
12:06.837 --> 12:07.879
How's your guy?

212
12:07.880 --> 12:09.339
Kiko?

213
12:10.883 --> 12:12.634
He's okay.

214
12:13.886 --> 12:18.348
Why didn't he come to your grandpa's funeral?

215
12:20.350 --> 12:21.893
He's busy.

216
12:21.894 --> 12:25.898
He has a lot to do tomorrow.

217
12:32.905 --> 12:33.906
Jorge?

218
12:40.329 --> 12:42.080
Forgive me.

219
12:44.750 --> 12:46.167
Dad.

220
12:46.168 --> 12:47.920
You're not at fault.

221
12:48.712 --> 12:50.422
We understand.

222
12:54.259 --> 12:55.636
Jorge.

223
12:57.012 --> 12:59.181
I'm sorry.

224
13:01.225 --> 13:04.602
I wasn't a good father to you.

225
13:04.603 --> 13:06.605
In any way.

226
13:13.237 --> 13:15.113
Dad.

227
13:16.532 --> 13:18.534
Forgive me too.

228
13:20.452 --> 13:22.621
Jorge.

229
13:24.998 --> 13:28.543
I couldn’t give you everything.

230
13:28.544 --> 13:32.004
As much as

231
13:32.005 --> 13:35.092
what your grandpa gave you.

232
13:42.558 --> 13:46.727
Aunt Lilia promised

233
13:46.728 --> 13:50.649
she will manage the restaurant.

234
13:52.651 --> 13:57.030
She will entrust it to me once I graduate.

235
13:58.282 --> 14:00.658
Or...

236
14:00.659 --> 14:04.162
I can manage our new branch.

237
14:12.796 --> 14:14.798
Son.

238
14:16.091 --> 14:18.676
I’m running out of time.

239
14:18.677 --> 14:22.221
I wish I could’ve left you with some guidance

240
14:22.222 --> 14:26.226
and opportunities for you to be happy.

241
14:28.770 --> 14:30.522
Dad.

242
14:32.983 --> 14:35.861
It's okay.

243
14:37.362 --> 14:40.198
Thank you.

244
14:43.118 --> 14:45.495
Thank you, my son.

245
15:10.103 --> 15:11.854
Will you board the bus?

246
15:11.855 --> 15:12.856
Bus?

247
15:13.774 --> 15:15.108
Later.

248
15:16.318 --> 15:17.319
Okay.

249
15:51.645 --> 15:55.232
I couldn't let you leave without saying goodbye.

250
15:57.651 --> 16:00.112
It's good to see you here, Jorge.

251
16:01.321 --> 16:04.073
I'm happy for you.

252
16:04.074 --> 16:05.784
Sincerely.

253
16:06.702 --> 16:08.245
Thank you.

254
16:09.955 --> 16:11.957
You do good there.

255
16:13.375 --> 16:15.167
I'll really do my best.

256
16:15.168 --> 16:19.631
If not, they'll remove my scholarship.

257
16:26.096 --> 16:27.596
What's this?

258
16:27.597 --> 16:30.099
I didn't want to send this to the post office

259
16:30.100 --> 16:32.686
because it might get lost.

260
16:34.062 --> 16:36.772
It's why I wanted to give it straight to you.

261
16:36.773 --> 16:38.149
You know, Jorge.

262
16:38.150 --> 16:40.276
We're luckier than our grandparents.

263
16:40.277 --> 16:41.111
There's Facebook.

264
16:41.111 --> 16:41.820
Viber.

265
16:41.820 --> 16:42.446
Twitter.

266
16:42.447 --> 16:44.030
Instagram.

267
16:44.031 --> 16:44.865
Line.

268
16:44.866 --> 16:46.323
There’s a lot.

269
16:46.324 --> 16:48.994
Do you have accounts for all of those?

270
16:49.369 --> 16:52.997
It’s impossible not to update each other, Jorge.

271
16:52.998 --> 16:54.707
Of course.

272
16:54.708 --> 16:57.377
You'll know immediately when I marry.

273
17:00.005 --> 17:01.131
Sorry.

274
17:01.631 --> 17:02.758
Bad joke.

275
17:05.343 --> 17:07.262
Bad joke.

276
17:09.431 --> 17:11.475
Will you board the bus or not?

277
17:12.893 --> 17:14.686
Only him.

278
17:17.355 --> 17:19.191
Only him.

279
17:30.952 --> 17:32.078
I have to go, Jorge.

280
17:32.079 --> 17:33.162
Yes.

281
17:33.163 --> 17:34.706
Go.

282
18:33.014 --> 18:35.683
For my dear Kiko,

283
18:35.684 --> 18:40.104
You didn't get a chance to read Grandpa Bong's letter to Grandpa Tino.

284
18:40.105 --> 18:43.650
But I did.

285
18:44.276 --> 18:47.904
It's too sad for me to repeat it.

286
18:48.613 --> 18:50.865
I realized it's hard to wait

287
18:50.866 --> 18:54.286
when you don't know if there's still something you're waiting for.

288
18:59.374 --> 19:01.877
So, I thought...

289
19:03.336 --> 19:05.505
I won't wait for you anymore.

290
19:07.090 --> 19:10.677
I won't wait many years for you.

291
19:11.261 --> 19:13.471
That’s why...

292
19:13.472 --> 19:16.183
I will follow you to Manila.

293
19:17.893 --> 19:21.687
I will study as well.

294
19:21.688 --> 19:23.814
I will follow you.

295
19:23.815 --> 19:25.858
So we could be together.

296
19:25.859 --> 19:28.195
Wait!

297
21:41.286 --> 21:43.412
Where's the lighter, Lilia?

298
21:43.413 --> 21:47.124
Here. Continue preparing there.

299
21:47.125 --> 21:48.125
Ruth!

300
21:48.126 --> 21:49.418
Yes, Auntie?

301
21:49.419 --> 21:50.836
Make sure...

302
21:50.837 --> 21:53.380
They will taste Jorge’s miki.

303
21:53.381 --> 21:55.424
So we could put it into the menu.

304
21:55.425 --> 21:57.092
Of course, Auntie.

305
21:57.093 --> 21:58.886
Jorge would love that.

306
21:58.887 --> 22:00.722
Lilia.

307
22:01.264 --> 22:02.848
I wrote everyone.

308
22:02.849 --> 22:05.559
But I have a problem. Her name is Socorro.

309
22:05.560 --> 22:07.436
Does it have one "r" or two?

310
22:07.437 --> 22:08.980
Two R’s.

311
22:25.538 --> 22:27.247
They're here!

312
22:27.248 --> 22:28.332
How was the travel?

313
22:28.333 --> 22:30.793
- How are you? - I’m good.

314
22:30.794 --> 22:32.711
Here, let me help you.

315
22:32.712 --> 22:34.756
Come inside.

316
22:43.056 --> 22:46.851
What are you doing?

317
22:47.644 --> 22:49.728
How are the people from Manila?

318
22:49.729 --> 22:51.522
We're okay, Auntie.

319
22:51.523 --> 22:52.523
Is it your semester break?

320
22:52.524 --> 22:54.441
Yes. It's our semester break.

321
22:54.442 --> 22:57.653
You arrived at the right time.

322
22:57.654 --> 23:00.697
- You're so pretty, Auntie. - The prayer will start soon.

323
23:00.698 --> 23:02.908
Of course.

324
23:02.909 --> 23:04.410
Did you eat already?

325
23:04.411 --> 23:06.870
Not yet. I'm really hungry.

326
23:06.871 --> 23:08.664
We'll go cook then.

327
23:08.665 --> 23:11.500
We'll prepare the food.

328
23:11.501 --> 23:12.127
Okay, Auntie.

329
23:12.128 --> 23:13.378
Okay!

330
23:24.848 --> 23:26.182
Jorge.

331
23:28.143 --> 23:29.144
Kiko.

332
23:31.938 --> 23:34.232
I prepared your room.

333
24:29.496 --> 24:31.539
I'm so tired.

334
24:44.469 --> 24:46.095
Jorge.

335
24:56.981 --> 24:58.942
What?

336
25:49.158 --> 25:50.326
Dad.

337
25:50.910 --> 25:51.661
What?

338
25:51.662 --> 25:52.954
Can I see that?

339
25:57.208 --> 25:58.751
May I borrow your pen?

340
26:11.889 --> 26:14.267
Who's Primitivo?

341
26:15.810 --> 26:18.021
Grandpa Tino's friend.

342
26:26.237 --> 26:28.156
What are you praying for?

343
26:31.200 --> 26:35.370
Can't I pray in silence so it will come true?

344
26:35.371 --> 26:38.332
Jorge, you're not blowing out candles on a cake.

345
26:38.333 --> 26:42.252
The dead are listening so they can help us get what we want.

346
26:42.253 --> 26:45.965
I'm just saying, you can tell me.

347
26:47.300 --> 26:50.093
Do I really have to tell you?

348
26:50.094 --> 26:51.219
Yes.

349
26:51.220 --> 26:53.681
Unless you already got what you wanted.

350
26:56.726 --> 26:58.101
Get inside.

351
26:58.102 --> 27:01.230
The prayer will start.

352
27:22.210 --> 27:24.670
In the name of the Father, the Son, the Holy Spirit.

353
27:24.671 --> 27:25.421
Amen.

354
27:25.422 --> 27:30.134
I believe in God, the Father Almighty...

355
27:49.153 --> 27:53.950
Our Father who art in Heaven...

356
27:56.911 --> 28:02.708
Blessed are the souls of those who enter your Kingdom.

357
28:02.709 --> 28:06.628
Eternal rest grant unto the soul

358
28:06.629 --> 28:08.547
for the soul of Socorro,

359
28:08.548 --> 28:10.424
for the soul of Teresa,

360
28:10.425 --> 28:15.304
for the soul of Primitivo, for the soul of Celestino...

361
28:25.500 --> 28:30.000
"All the Things I Leave You"
